## 2. Door Control (门控)

### BCM-DOOR-001: Door Lock Control
- The system SHALL lock all doors within 150 ms of receiving a lock request via CAN
- The system SHALL unlock individual doors based on the CAN message payload
- The system SHALL provide feedback via CAN indicating the lock status
- The system SHALL activate child lock within 200 ms of request

### BCM-DOOR-002: Window Lift Control
- The system SHALL control each window lift motor independently
- The system SHALL support one-touch auto-up and auto-down with pinch protection
- The system SHALL stop window movement immediately when pinch detection exceeds threshold
- The system SHALL store pinch calibration values in NVM

### BCM-DOOR-003: Mirror Control
- The system SHALL adjust mirror position (horizontal/vertical) based on LIN commands
- The system SHALL store mirror position presets in NVM
- The system SHALL fold mirrors automatically when vehicle is locked

### BCM-DOOR-004: Door Status Monitoring
- The system SHALL detect door open/close state for each door via Hall sensors
- The system SHALL publish door status on CAN every 100 ms
- The system SHALL detect ajar state and trigger warning after 30 seconds

---

## 3. Light Control (灯光)

### BCM-LIGHT-001: Headlight Control
- The system SHALL control low beam and high beam actuators via PWM
- The system SHALL support automatic headlight leveling
- The system SHALL switch between low/high beam within 50 ms of command
- The system SHALL activate daytime running lights (DRL) when engine is running

### BCM-LIGHT-002: Turn Signal Control
- The system SHALL control left/right turn signals with 50% duty cycle at 1.5 Hz
- The system SHALL support hazard warning (both turn signals simultaneously)
- The system SHALL detect bulb failure via current monitoring and report via CAN

### BCM-LIGHT-003: Interior Lighting
- The system SHALL control interior ambient light dimming with PWM
- The system SHALL support scenario-based lighting (door open → interior lights on)
- The system SHALL fade interior lights in/out over 500 ms

### BCM-LIGHT-004: Brake Light
- The system SHALL activate brake lights within 50 ms of brake pedal detection
- The system SHALL support emergency brake flash (rapid flashing at >0.6g deceleration)

---

## 4. Wiper Control (雨刮)

### BCM-WIPER-001: Wiper Speed Control
- The system SHALL control wiper motor at low speed, high speed, and intermittent modes
- The system SHALL support intermittent delay adjustment (2s, 4s, 6s, 8s, 10s)
- The system SHALL auto-park wipers at the rest position when turned off

### BCM-WIPER-002: Rain Sensor Integration
- The system SHALL read rain sensor data via LIN interface
- The system SHALL automatically activate wipers when rain is detected above threshold
- The system SHALL adjust wiper speed proportionally to rainfall intensity

### BCM-WIPER-003: Wash-Wipe Function
- The system SHALL activate washer pump for 1.5 seconds on command
- The system SHALL perform 3 wipe cycles after washer activation
- The system SHALL support rear window wiper and washer

---

## 5. Power Management (电源管理)

### BCM-PWR-001: Power Mode Management
- The system SHALL support SLEEP, RUN, and STOP power modes per AUTOSAR ECU State Manager
- The system SHALL transition to SLEEP mode within 500 ms of sleep request
- The system SHALL wake from SLEEP on CAN activity, LIN activity, or digital input

### BCM-PWR-002: KL15 and KL30 Monitoring
- The system SHALL monitor KL15 (ignition) and KL30 (battery) voltage levels
- The system SHALL report undervoltage (< 8V) and overvoltage (> 16V) via DTC
- The system SHALL perform graceful shutdown when KL15 is OFF for > 3 seconds

### BCM-PWR-003: Low Power Consumption
- The system SHALL consume less than 100 µA in SLEEP mode
- The system SHALL complete wake-up to operational state within 50 ms
- The system SHALL support timed wake-up (RTC alarm)

---

## 6. Safety Requirements

### BCM-SAF-001: MPU Protection (ASIL B)
{% if asil == 'ASIL_B' or asil == 'ASIL_C' or asil == 'ASIL_D' %}
- The system SHALL configure MPU to protect safety-critical memory regions
- The system SHALL detect and report MPU violations via DEM
- The system SHALL isolate SWC memory regions using MPU partitions
{% else %}
- The system SHOULD configure MPU to protect memory regions
- The system MAY detect and report memory access violations
{% endif %}

### BCM-SAF-002: Watchdog Supervision
- The system SHALL configure the hardware watchdog with a timeout of 100 ms
- The system SHALL trigger Alive Supervision for all runnable entities
- The system SHALL trigger Deadline Supervision for time-critical SWCs
- The system SHALL perform an ECU reset if watchdog triggers

### BCM-SAF-003: End-to-End Protection
- The system SHALL implement E2E profile 1 for safety-critical CAN signals
- The system SHALL detect data corruption, repetition, loss, and delay
- The system SHALL report E2E errors to DEM with DTC

### BCM-SAF-004: Safe State
- The system SHALL enter safe state (all outputs to pre-defined safe values) on safety violation
- The system SHALL log the safety violation event in DEM before entering safe state
- The system SHALL remain in safe state until external reset

