## 7. Acceptance Scenarios

### Scenario: Door Lock/Unlock Cycle
- GIVEN the system is in RUN mode
- WHEN a CAN lock command is received for all doors
- THEN all door actuators SHALL engage lock within 150 ms
- AND a CAN status message SHALL be sent confirming locked state
- WHEN an unlock command is received for driver door
- THEN only the driver door actuator SHALL disengage lock

### Scenario: Light Switch Cycle
- GIVEN the system is in RUN mode
- WHEN low beam command is received
- THEN headlight PWM output SHALL activate within 50 ms
- AND the response CAN message SHALL indicate low beam ON
- WHEN turn signal left command is received
- THEN left turn signal SHALL flash at 1.5 Hz with 50% duty cycle

### Scenario: Wiper Rain Detection
- GIVEN the wiper mode is AUTO
- WHEN rain sensor detects precipitation above threshold
- THEN wipers SHALL activate at calculated speed within 200 ms
- AND the wiper status SHALL be reported on CAN

### Scenario: Sleep/Wake Cycle
- GIVEN KL15 is OFF and no CAN activity for 5 seconds
- WHEN the system receives a sleep request
- THEN the system SHALL transition to SLEEP mode within 500 ms
- WHEN a CAN message is received
- THEN the system SHALL wake and return to RUN mode within 50 ms
